# Negative test: gmeow:gmnGlyphInScope and gmeow:gmnGlyphNamedKeyRuled PARTITION the
# logic-glyph-plane terms — a term is EITHER in scope for a rendered glyph OR ruled to a
# named key where no standard notation exists, never both. The coverage gate
# (gmn-logic-coverage-complete) reads the in-scope set MINUS the named-key-ruled set as its
# coverage denominator on the assumption the two markers are disjoint; a term carrying BOTH
# would be silently excused from the coverage anti-join (the named-key filter would exempt an
# in-scope term that still owes a rendering). Any returned row is a term that breaks the
# partition. The shipped graph marks each term with at most one of the two, so this returns
# no rows.
PREFIX gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/>

SELECT ?t WHERE {
    ?t gmeow:gmnGlyphInScope true ;
       gmeow:gmnGlyphNamedKeyRuled true .
}
ORDER BY ?t
